# Unreal legacy OBJ adapter: canonical vertices are centimetres in the bird frame (+X forward, +Y right, +Z up, origin at the body centre); this file is written with Y reflected and triangle winding reversed. One object, exactly two g groups (plumage_main, plumage_hood), so the importer creates exactly two material slots.
# Rock dove (feral pigeon) (Columba livia), pose down_stroke
# wingspan 67.0 cm, body length 33.0 cm; Collins Bird Guide 2nd ed. (Svensson, Mullarney & Zetterstrom, 2009), Columba livia: length 30-35 cm, wingspan 62-72 cm; same range in Cramp (ed.), Birds of the Western Palearctic vol. IV. Mid-points used: 33 cm and 67 cm.
# AUTHORED low-poly silhouette in those published proportions. Not a scan, not photogrammetry, not a claim about an individual bird.
